================================================================================
SYSTEMD EXECUTION SERVICE — SUPPORT FILE
================================================================================
ROLE:
    This service runs the Ardhanarishvara Autonomous Execution Engine as a
    persistent system daemon. It ensures the engine starts on boot, restarts
    on failure, and logs output to the /logs directory.

SERVICE NAME:
    ardhanarishvara-execution.service

KEY FEATURES:
    - Auto-starts on boot
    - Auto-restarts on crash
    - Uses DISPLAY=:2 for Xvfb
    - Uses Python virtual environment
    - Logs stdout and stderr to /logs
    - Runs under user: keshanth

FILES:
    /etc/systemd/system/ardhanarishvara-execution.service
    /home/keshanth/ARKA/ardhanarishvara/logs/execution.log
    /home/keshanth/ARKA/ardhanarishvara/logs/execution.err

COMMANDS:
    sudo systemctl daemon-reload
    sudo systemctl enable ardhanarishvara-execution.service
    sudo systemctl start ardhanarishvara-execution.service
    systemctl status ardhanarishvara-execution.service

NOTES:
    - Ensure Xvfb is running on :2 before starting the service.
    - Ensure IB Gateway is running and authenticated.
    - Ensure kill.switch file is absent unless intentionally halting the engine.

================================================================================
END OF SUPPORT FILE
================================================================================
